but an initial agent prompt remains visible until the full run finishes. `ActionAgentPrompt` resets only when the controller changes `promptResetToken`.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_1_0\\\\F_113_only_show_responses_when_in_waitforinput_mode.md:23:Response prompts are the selected action's `phrases`. `ActionPhraseButtonsOwner` shows them for any agent follow-up: while the scoped run is queued, running, or `waitingForInput`, and after the run when a stored conversation can continue. Therefore they can appear as soon as a run starts and outside the period when the agent awaits user input.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_1_0\\\\F_113_only_show_responses_when_in_waitforinput_mode.md:25:`ActionPopupContent` renders the phrase buttons as a separate row after the prompt area. The row consumes popup height instead of floating over the prompt. Selecting a phrase replaces the prompt draft; double-clicking also submits it.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_1_0\\\\F_113_only_show_responses_when_in_waitforinput_mode.md:30:- Keep response prompts limited to agent actions with at least one phrase. Hide them during idle, queued, running, and terminal states.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_1_0\\\\F_113_only_show_responses_when_in_waitforinput_mode.md:39:- Response prompts are absent before the run waits, including while it is queued or running.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_3\\\\F_78_uniform_agent_controls_and_auto_finish.md:47:- Use one icon-only Stop control for every running agent action. Accessible label and tooltip: `Stop`.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_1_0\\\\F_110_card_action_popup_should_show_card_id.md:5:title: card-action popup should show card id\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_1_0\\\\F_110_card_action_popup_should_show_card_id.md:22:`ActionPopupContent` renders action, worktree, conversation, expand, and close controls in its header, but no target identity. Its accessible title is always `Run actions`.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_1_0\\\\F_110_card_action_popup_should_show_card_id.md:24:Card popups keep `cardInternalId` in `ActionContext`; `ActionPopup` already subscribes to project state, where the matching card exposes its user-facing `header.id`. Project-agent popups use context kind `project`.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_1_0\\\\F_110_card_action_popup_should_show_card_id.md:34:- Every card action popup visibly shows its card ID in the header.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_3\\\\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:16:- `handleClose()` is the only terminal path: persists conversation, releases `runningConversationIds`, calls `onComplete`.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_3\\\\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:56:  - `runningConversationIds` guard, conversation persistence, and `onComplete` all hang off `handleClose`; each needs a streaming-aware trigger.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_3\\\\F_76_action_streaming_or_oneshot_agent_mode.md:74:- Long-lived child processes: leaks, zombie `runningConversationIds`, cancel semantics on app quit.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\card__05d5d49c-401f-42cd-b3cc-074e169631dd.json:38:          \\\"type\\\": \\\"reasoning\\\"\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\card__05d5d49c-401f-42cd-b3cc-074e169631dd.json:110:          \\\"type\\\": \\\"reasoning\\\"\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\card__05d5d49c-401f-42cd-b3cc-074e169631dd.json:146:          \\\"output\\\": \\\"1\\\\t---\\\\n2\\\\tauthor: \\\\n3\\\\tid: F_153\\\\n4\\\\tinternalId: 05d5d49c-401f-42cd-b3cc-074e169631dd\\\\n5\\\\ttitle: action part in approval required\\\\n6\\\\tstatus: design\\\\n7\\\\towner: \\\\n8\\\\taffects:\\\\n9\\\\tagents:\\\\n10\\\\t  - design/activity/card__05d5d49c-401f-42cd-b3cc-074e169631dd.json#conversation=agent-2322e64a-9c75-4d08-b6cd-9b3d966b498b\\\\n11\\\\t  - design/activity/card__05d5d49c-401f-42cd-b3cc-074e169631dd.json#conversation=agent-793ef4cc-80b6-453e-a264-fc5869fdf065\\\\n12\\\\tpolicy:\\\\n13\\\\t---\\\\n14\\\\tThis is the text shown in the drawer shown when an agent requests for approval:\\\\n15\\\\t\\\\n16\\\\t> Approval requ